!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = treatment: vehicle (DMSO:EtOH)
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = time: 1h
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = genotype: wt
!Sample_molecule_ch1 = genomic DNA
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = Cells were counted and 50,000 cells were collected in ice-cold PBS. The nuclei were isolated with ATAC lysis buffer (10 mM Tris–HCl pH 7.4, 10 mM NaCl, 3 mM MgCl2, and 0.1% IGEPAL). Tagmentation of the nuclei was performed using the Tagment DNA TDE1 Enzyme and Buffer Kits (Illumina). Indexing was performed using Nextera DNA library preparation kit (Illumina). DNA was purified with NucleoSpin Gel and PCR Clean-up Kit (Macherey-Nagel). Indexed DNA was amplified for nine PCR cycles with Kapa Hifi Hot Start Kit (Kapa Biosystems). Amplified libraries were purified again with NucleoSpin Gel and PCR Clean-up Kit (Macherey-Nagel).
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = Indexed libraries were prepared from tagmented DNA, using Nextera DNA library preparation kit (Illumina)
!Sample_data_processing = alignment with bwa using default parameters
!Sample_data_processing = bam generation with Picard tools using SortSam, AddOrreplaceReadGroups, CollectAlignmentSummaryMetrics, CollectInsertSizeMetrics, MarkDuplicates with default parameters
!Sample_data_processing = tag directory generation with HOMER makeTagDirectory
!Sample_data_processing = Model-based analysis of ChIP-seq version 2 (MACS2) was used for predicting summits of the peaks using q value cutoff (q) = 0.001.
!Sample_data_processing = Assembly: hg38
!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary files format and content: bedgraph
